  "contractAddressNote": "The address of the deployment this scenario drives. It is a function of the NEF, the manifest name and the deploy signer, so the receipt records the address the engine actually deployed and requires it to equal this one.",
  "note": [
    "An ordered list of calls with literal arguments over one deployment. This file says what to call; the dump says what happened. It is input, never evidence.",
    "The account id below is the value computeRegistrationAccountId derives for these parameters. It is pinned here as a literal so that every step's script bytes are a function of this file alone, and the compute step is joined to it by readsForward so a wrong literal is caught before it is used. registerAccount independently recomputes the id and faults on a mismatch.",
    "The pinned id is the address form. Neo stores a Hash160 little-endian, so the value an ABI call receives, and the bytes a call returns, are both the reverse of that display hex. The compute step's result therefore reads as the reverse of the literal below, and the readsForward link compares stack bytes with stack bytes.",
    "A step that expects FAULT is placed only after the writes later steps read, because this harness shares one storage snapshot across steps and does not roll a faulting step back.",
    "The user operations name the contract under test as their target, so the execution phase calls back into this same deployment while its own execution lock is set."
  ],
